dence_ids":["link.quartic.proposition-3"],"id":"quartic.proposition-3","kind":"claim","label":"Proposition 3","locator":"Proposition 3, Section 4.2","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Proposition 3** (OpenAI ([OpenAI 2026](#cite-OpenAI2026), Proposition 3.2)). *Let $T=\\lceil\\log(1000m)\\rceil$ and $\\varepsilon=1/(1000T)$. Suppose a reversible comparison circuit, controlled by two candidate indices, uses at most $c$ queries and satisfies (4). There is a quantum algorithm making $O(c\\sqrt m\\,T^2\\log T)$ queries on every branch and returning a list of at most $T$ candidates such that, if $a_{i^\\star j}\\ge1-\\varepsilon$ for all $j\\ne i^\\star$, the list contains $i^\\star$ with probability at least $1-2m2^{-T}-T\\varepsilon$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.proposition-3","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.proposition-3","id":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/edges/%5B%22quartic.proposition-3%22%2C%22lean.QuarticQuery.Paper.quantumTournament%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/edges/%5B%22quartic.proposition-3%22%2C%22lean.QuarticQuery.Paper.quantumTournament%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/lean.QuarticQuery.Paper.quantumTournament"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.proposition-3","id":"field:26052ef2b3d6542d318b3b6038ba76d1fc276e8da0fb3e850e6ee74bc3ba6344","kind":"source_id","owner_ref":"sha256:b01fb7dc64f90c9c1f9fb29554b974330c989197a18a158ed14e47c792db1a40/nodes/quartic.proposition-3","semantic_class":"provenanc